@inject ApiMetadata Api

@* Stepper's Overview, written by hand after the selection Overviews: a checkout (the demo, in a
   frame with a phone width), vertical with descriptions, a step that only sometimes applies, sizes,
   and the ends. Parts, Accessibility and See also come from the metadata and the doc
   comments. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A stepper shows where the user is in a process, such as a checkout or a setup wizard. It's an ordered list that works <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">with JavaScript off</Anchor>, so it looks the same on every page. Your page sets which step is <Code>Current</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Steps of a checkout</Heading>
<TextBlock>The current step is the one the user is on, counting from 1, and the steps before it show as done. Set <Code>Current</Code>. To make a step's label a link, such as back to a finished step, set the <Code>Step</Code>'s <Code>Href</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="stepper-checkout" WidthSwitch />
<TextBlock>This example keeps the step in the URL as <Code>?step=</Code>. Each step's form moves on to the next step once it's valid: with a form post on static pages, and in C# on interactive pages. So it works with JavaScript off too.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Below 640px, the steps stay a row of markers, and only the current step's label shows. A finished step's link is still there, on its marker.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Vertical, with descriptions</Heading>
<TextBlock>A vertical stepper keeps the steps in a column on every screen. Set <Code>Orientation="Orientation.Vertical"</Code>. To add a line under a step's label, set the <Code>Step</Code>'s <Code>Description</Code>; to show an icon in its marker until the step is done, set its <Code>Icon</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="stepper-vertical" />

<Heading Level="2">A step that only sometimes applies</Heading>
<TextBlock>Some steps apply only sometimes, such as a gift message. To leave out a step that doesn't apply this time, set its <Code>Hidden</Code>. The steps after it are numbered to match.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="stepper-optional" />
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Hidden</Code> rather than <Code>@@if</Code>. On interactive pages, Blazor renders a step that appears later after the others, so it would be numbered last.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes</Heading>
<TextBlock>The size scales the markers and the text with the buttons and fields around them. Set <Code>Size</Code> to choose one.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="stepper-sizes" />

<Heading Level="2">Before the first step and after the last</Heading>
<TextBlock>A stepper can show that no step has started yet, or that every step is done. When no step has started, set <Code>Current="0"</Code>. To show every step done, such as on an order's confirmation, set a number past the last step.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The list has a name for screen readers, and a finished step has a word in place of its check mark. To set them for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Label</Code></td><td>The list's name</td><td>"Progress"</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>CompletedLabel</Code></td><td>What screen readers hear after a finished step's label, in place of its check mark</td><td>"(completed)"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Stepper Current="2" Label="Sign-up progress">
            <Step Label="Account" Href="/signup/account" />
            <Step Label="Profile" Description="Name and photo" />
            <Step Label="Done" />
        </Stepper>
        """;
}
